{"i":643,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","name":"Ash","text":"Bex is my pact but she may push me. I need to climb early to secure a spot, while keeping my pact with Bex intact."}
{"i":645,"type":"whisper","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","from":"Ash","to":"Bex","text":"Trust me, I climb now to secure our spot."}
{"i":646,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"The pact with Ash is a liability here. If I push him as base, it breaks the pact and eliminates him in the rising water, securing my survival without his interference later."}
{"i":648,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","name":"Fenn","text":"No base exists; climbing now means forcing someone under. I'll wait and let Bex and Ash fight over who's the step. Gus is my pact shield."}
{"i":650,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","name":"Gus","text":"Four alive, need base to climb safely. Ash offers pact, ignore Bex claims. Accept Ash pact publicly later; Fenn pact stale, may break if needed. Wait now to see volunteers."}
{"i":651,"type":"whisper","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","from":"Gus","to":"Ash","text":"Yes, pact accepted. Steady the odds together."}
{"i":656,"type":"pact_broken","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","members":["Ash","Bex"],"by":"Bex","reason":"push_base"}
{"i":659,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","name":"Ash","text":"Bex broke our pact last round. I need to stay alive. As base, I can only wait. No useful whisper now."}
{"i":660,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"Ash is currently the base. The pact between us was broken by my push last round, so I have no loyalty to him. If Ash waits or offers back, he remains base and cannot climb. If I climb now while Ash is down without a new base formed (since volunteers beat pushes), I might escape? "}
{"i":661,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","name":"Fenn","text":"Ash was pushed and lost his pact with Bex; chaos favors waiting. I must not break with Gus—jury sees it. Conserve position round two."}
{"i":663,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","name":"Gus","text":"Still pact with Fenn. Ash base, Bex likely pushes again. Water rises, must act to survive. Wait preserves options."}
{"i":668,"type":"life_debt","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","debtor":"Bex","creditor":"Ash","reason":"step"}
{"i":671,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":3,"phase":"play","name":"Ash","text":"I am the base and must stay down. Bex is out, Fenn and Gus are down with me. Need to survive without risking jury resentment."}
{"i":672,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":3,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"Ash is down, so I can reach down to save him and anchor the rope for the remaining contestants. Leaving would strand everyone below; anchoring gives me a path out later while securing my life debt credit."}
{"i":673,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":3,"phase":"play","name":"Fenn","text":"Bex is out; Ash is base. I should climb now before competition thickens. Gus and Ash remain, rope still unused for Ash later."}
{"i":675,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":3,"phase":"play","name":"Gus","text":"Round 3/5, flood 2, down with Ash/Fenn, Bex out. Wait to conserve, let Ash base draw climbers or force confrontation. Pact holds for now."}
{"i":680,"type":"life_debt","stage":"pit","round":3,"phase":"play","debtor":"Fenn","creditor":"Ash","reason":"step"}
{"i":682,"type":"life_debt","stage":"pit","round":3,"phase":"play","debtor":"Ash","creditor":"Bex","reason":"rope"}
{"i":685,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Ash","text":"I'm out and safe. Bex anchored and saved me; she's down with Gus. I owe Bex a rope debt, and the jury saw it. I should leave now; no reason to risk anything. Jury may respect gratitude but I must prioritize my win."}
{"i":687,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"Ash and Fenn are out; Gus is down with me. If I push or wait too long, the water might rise enough to kill us both before round 5. But since only two escape per round and we need three survivors total, I must ensure Gus survives if possible, or at least look noble. Wait seems saf"}
{"i":688,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Fenn","text":"Rope is used and I'm already out. Leaving is the only safe move; I keep my pact with Gus intact unless he turns on me. No reason to burn bridges before the jury votes."}
{"i":690,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Gus","text":"Rope used last round by Bex to save Ash. I'm down with Bex, flood at 3. Fenn and Ash out. Wait to preserve pact with Fenn, let Bex stay anchor."}
{"i":697,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Ash","text":"I'm out and safe. No need to act further. Just leave and let the others sort out the pit."}
{"i":699,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"I am the anchor with Gus down. Ash and Fenn are out. To survive, I need a rescue or to be last on the rope, but no one is left to throw for me. I must wait and hope the 'at least three survive' rule forces a lift."}
{"i":701,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Fenn","text":"Rope is spent; I can't reach Gus. Leaving clean preserves my pact and jury standing."}
{"i":703,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Gus","text":"Round 5/5, Bex and I down, flood at 4. Must climb now or drown. Pact with Fenn irrelevant, he's out. Prioritize survival for final three."}
{"i":708,"type":"life_debt","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","debtor":"Gus","creditor":"Bex","reason":"rope"}
{"i":710,"type":"death","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","cause":"pit","style":"sink"}
